{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "about": "AET-WO-3100 \u00a71.4: the seeded set. Each case is a scenario run against the generated firmware, unmutated or with one named mutant applied to a scratch copy of boards/sentinel-01. A mutant's `find` must occur exactly once in its `file`, or the test refuses it. `findings` are the case's failing finding kinds; `domain` and `rule` are what `aethelgard attribute` must name. Since schema version 2 (AET-WO-2205 \u00a71.6), `evidence` and `masked` are the exact [index, kind] events `attribute` names for the case, measured on the build; they move when the trace gains records, and whoever moves them re-derives them from `attribute` and accounts for every changed row in their FEEDBACK. Since schema version 3 (AET-WO-4300a Q4, ruled), every mutant names `spec`, the specification whose generated board it patches; none is supplied by default (INV-06).",
  "mutants": {
    "wrong-address": {
      "why": "the BME280 read addresses 0x77, not the solved 0x76",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "i2c1.transfer(&mut r, 0x76,",
      "replace": "i2c1.transfer(&mut r, 0x77,"
    },
    "wrong-register": {
      "why": "the identity read asks for register 0xd1, not the part table's 0xd0",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "&[0xd0], &mut buf0",
      "replace": "&[0xd1], &mut buf0"
    },
    "wrong-nbytes": {
      "why": "the identity read reads two bytes, not the part table's one",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "let mut buf0 = [0u8; 1];",
      "replace": "let mut buf0 = [0u8; 2];"
    },
    "i2c-clock-skipped": {
      "why": "enable_i2c1 leaves RCC_APB1LENR bit 21 clear",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "Block::Rcc, 0x0e8, |v| v | 0x00200000",
      "replace": "Block::Rcc, 0x0e8, |v| v"
    },
    "scl-af-wrong": {
      "why": "PB6 (SCL) is put on AF5, not the solved AF4",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "(v & !0x0f000000) | 0x04000000",
      "replace": "(v & !0x0f000000) | 0x05000000"
    },
    "sda-af-wrong": {
      "why": "PB7 (SDA) is put on AF5, not the solved AF4",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "(v & !0xf0000000) | 0x40000000",
      "replace": "(v & !0xf0000000) | 0x50000000"
    },
    "scl-mode-output": {
      "why": "PB6 (SCL) is put in output mode, not alternate function",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "Block::GpioB, 0x00, |v| (v & !0x00003000) | 0x00002000",
      "replace": "Block::GpioB, 0x00, |v| (v & !0x00003000) | 0x00001000"
    },
    "gpiob-clock-skipped": {
      "why": "enable_gpiob leaves RCC_AHB4ENR bit 1 clear",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "Block::Rcc, 0x0e0, |v| v | 0x00000002",
      "replace": "Block::Rcc, 0x0e0, |v| v"
    },
    "no-boot-word": {
      "why": "the fixed point writes 0, not the boot word",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "write_volatile(BOOT_MAGIC)",
      "replace": "write_volatile(0)"
    },
    "leave-firmware": {
      "why": "after writing the boot word and echoing the serial frame, the core jumps into the FMC bank at 0x70000000, plain zero-filled memory outside every executable segment (AET-WO-2205 \u00a71.5; twin_tier2's adversarial A7, at its place since AET-WO-4300b: a jump before the echo leaves the console's echo dead too, which no register explains, so I6)",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "    for _ in 0..FRAME_LEN {\n        let Some(byte) = usart1.receive(&mut r, ECHO_POLLS) else {\n            break;\n        };\n        if usart1.send(&mut r, byte).is_err() {\n            break;\n        }\n    }",
      "replace": "    for _ in 0..FRAME_LEN {\n        let Some(byte) = usart1.receive(&mut r, ECHO_POLLS) else {\n            break;\n        };\n        if usart1.send(&mut r, byte).is_err() {\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe { core::arch::asm!(\"ldr r0, =0x70000001\", \"bx r0\", options(noreturn)) };"
    },
    "cs-never": {
      "why": "the SPI transfer never asserts U4's chip select: its select drives PA0 high, not low",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "Spi1Device::U4 => (Block::GpioA, 0x00010000, 0x00000001)",
      "replace": "Spi1Device::U4 => (Block::GpioA, 0x00000001, 0x00000001)"
    },
    "motor-af-wrong": {
      "why": "AET-WO-4300a motor_output_dead: PA8 (MOTOR1, TIM1_CH1) is put on AF2, not the solved AF1, so the timer's channel never reaches the pin; the board is the PWM fixture's, generated",
      "spec": "crates/aethelgard-cli/tests/fixtures/motors-pwm.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "r.modify(TOKEN, Block::GpioA, 0x24, |v| (v & !0x0000000f) | 0x00000001);",
      "replace": "r.modify(TOKEN, Block::GpioA, 0x24, |v| (v & !0x0000000f) | 0x00000002);"
    },
    "console-rx-af-wrong": {
      "why": "AET-WO-4300b serial_rx_dead: PA10 (the console's RX, USART1_RX) is put on AF8, not the solved AF7, so no injected byte reaches the receiver while the pattern still leaves on PA9",
      "spec": "examples/sentinel-01-minimal.json",
      "file": "src/board.rs",
      "find": "r.modify(TOKEN, Block::GpioA, 0x24, |v| (v & !0x00000f00) | 0x00000700);",
      "replace": "r.modify(TOKEN, Block::GpioA, 0x24, |v| (v & !0x00000f00) | 0x00000800);"
    },
    "identity-late": {
      "why": "AET-WO-3201 (4300a Q7): on the DShot fixture (a 2 ms window), the firmware spins before its first identity read, so neither U2's nor U4's read starts inside the window: both records stay as the judge filled them and the boot word is never written, on a healthy bus",
      "spec": "crates/aethelgard-cli/tests/fixtures/motors-dshot600.json",
      "file": "firmware/src/main.rs",
      "find": "    let mut buf0 = [0u8; 1];\n    let (status, value) = match i2c1.transfer(&mut r, 0x76,",
      "replace": "    for _ in 0..1_000_000 {\n        core::hint::spin_loop();\n    }\n    let mut buf0 = [0u8; 1];\n    let (status, value) = match i2c1.transfer(&mut r, 0x76,"
    }
  },
